{% if relations_correct %}## Whether each relation the run asserted holds

The objects are settled by what the scan was segmented into; the relations are what the
pipeline adds, so they are judged one at a time rather than counted. A relation is correct
when the modelled world holds the part anywhere inside the matched whole: a run that hangs a
drawer straight off the island rather than off the cabinet inside it has still put it
somewhere it really is.

