{% if placement %}## Whether each part is in the right piece of furniture

Asked of pairs of parts rather than of a part and its whole, so no predicted cabinet has to
be declared the same object as a modelled one -- a run that finds one cabinet as five
fragments has no such answer. {{ matching.matched | length }} of {{ matching.matched | length + matching.unmatched_predicted | length }} run objects were paired with a modelled one, and {{ placement.considered | length }} of those are parts held by something.

A part is judged by the **outermost** whole it ends up in, not by the one that directly
holds it. The modelled world nests deeper than the question does -- it puts a drawer inside
a cabinet inside a side, while the run builds one island holding cabinets, countertop and
drawers at a single level -- and judging by the immediate whole scores that flattening as
misplacement.

**Placement {{ "%.2f" | format(placement.pairs.precision) }}** -- of the {{ placement.pairs.predicted }} pairs of parts the run put in one piece of
furniture, {{ placement.pairs.in_both }} belong in one piece of furniture.
